Lab 6: Linear Regression on Ecommerce Customers Dataset

In this lab, I applied linear regression to the Ecommerce Customers dataset.

Steps performed
- Loaded the dataset into a DataFrame
- Explored the data using `head()`, `info()`, and `describe()`
- Checked for missing values and duplicate rows
- Confirmed that no basic data cleaning was needed
- Did not apply feature engineering because the dataset already contained suitable numerical features
- Prepared the data for modeling by selecting the input features and target variable
- Split the data into training and testing sets
- Trained a Linear Regression model
- Evaluated the model using regression metrics

Features used
- Avg. Session Length
- Time on App
- Time on Website
- Length of Membership

Target variable
- Yearly Amount Spent

Model evaluation results
- **MAE:** 7.74
- **MSE:** 93.83
- **RMSE:** 9.69

## Conclusion
The linear regression model performed well on the Ecommerce Customers dataset.  
The RMSE value shows that the model’s predictions are close to the actual yearly amount spent, with an average error of about 9.69 units.
